#4471 was marked as one known parser problem. Its export contains 412 unique reports, but the
tenant and booking-form data split them into two independently fixable causes.

## Split tickets

<Incident4471Split />

## Why these are separate

### Shared parser

Every tenant in this incident writes dates day first. The shared parser reads those dates month
first, so a valid day-first date can land on the wrong calendar day. This is the parser ticket.

### booking-v3 date hint

Three day-first tenants use `booking-v3`. Its date field displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, so people enter a
month-first value that the tenant-locale form then interprets day first. This is a form-hint ticket,
not the shared parser defect.

## Method

The export repeats 15 rows, so report IDs were deduplicated before counting. Each unique report was
classified from its tenant locale, booking form, and intake channel using `causeOf` in
`src/lib/kb/causes.ts`.

